{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart@navapbc.com","data":{"fields":{"description":"The archive-massgov-pfml checks entry runs the whole jest suite on every agent run, though the comment above it claims only the tests covering the changed page run. A pre-existing date-dependent failure in tests/features/status/PaymentIntroPrepaidCard.test.tsx, unrelated to any agent diff, therefore failed CI for execution intake-f6f13c6b. The repair loop spent 105 LLM calls and 3.2M tokens trying to fix a test the agent never touched, exhausted the budget, and parked the ticket in AWAITING_HUMAN with finished, correct work sitting on the branch.\n\nThe platform declares no build-tool convention, so it must not choose a test selector. It should instead tell the project which paths changed and let the declared command decide what to run. Thread the ticket file_impact paths from the workflow into the checks activity and the repair activity, expose them to the declared command as a CHANGED_PATHS environment variable in both the checks pod and the fix pod, and update the archive-massgov-pfml entry to pass them to jest --findRelatedTests with a full-suite fallback when the variable is empty.\n\nBoth ChecksSpec consumers must be threaded. The repair activity builds a ChecksSpec for run_fix, whose verify step re-runs the same declared command, so leaving it unthreaded would run the full suite during verification and reintroduce the defect.\n\nCHANGED_PATHS is serialized as a newline separated list, shell quoted as a single value, so a path containing a space survives. The declared command reads it with a NUL delimited xargs rather than bare word splitting.\n\nVerified against the promoted branch: jest --findRelatedTests over the five file_impact paths selects exactly the three suites the change affects, all of which pass, and excludes the unrelated failure.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] ChecksSpec accepts a changed_paths field, proven by `pytest tests/unit/test_checks_runner.py -k spec_changed_paths`\n- [ ] The checks pod script exports CHANGED_PATHS to the declared command when paths are given, proven by `pytest tests/unit/test_checks_runner.py -k exports_changed_paths`\n- [ ] The checks pod script omits the export when no paths are given, proven by `pytest tests/unit/test_checks_runner.py -k omits_changed_paths`\n- [ ] The exported value is newline separated and shell quoted so a path containing a space survives, proven by `pytest tests/unit/test_checks_runner.py -k changed_paths_quoting`\n- [ ] The fix pod script exports CHANGED_PATHS so the verify step stays scoped, proven by `pytest tests/unit/test_checks_runner.py -k fix_exports_changed_paths`\n- [ ] The run_checks activity forwards RunChecksRequest.changed_paths into ChecksSpec, proven by `pytest tests/unit/test_checks_runner.py -k forwards_changed_paths`\n- [ ] The apply_ci_repair activity forwards ApplyCIRepairRequest.changed_paths into ChecksSpec, proven by `pytest tests/unit/test_checks_runner.py -k repair_forwards_changed_paths`\n- [ ] The draft pull request workflow forwards ticket file_impact into RunChecksRequest, proven by `pytest tests/unit/test_draft_pull_request_workflow.py -k checks_changed_paths`\n- [ ] The draft pull request workflow forwards ticket file_impact into ApplyCIRepairRequest, proven by `pytest tests/unit/test_draft_pull_request_workflow.py -k repair_changed_paths`\n- [ ] The archive-massgov-pfml checks command scopes jest to CHANGED_PATHS, checked: reading the --findRelatedTests invocation in config/local/checks.yaml\n- [ ] The archive-massgov-pfml checks command falls back to the full suite when CHANGED_PATHS is empty, checked: reading the fallback branch in config/local/checks.yaml\n\n## Testing\nRun `pytest tests/unit/test_checks_runner.py tests/unit/test_draft_pull_request_workflow.py -q` to prove the threading and the export behaviour, then `ruff check .` for lint."}},"env_id":"8c3ef925-fbdc-4d88-8d59-f391cf59568c","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1789951047047023001,"uuid":"a4d8204b-f519-4be6-9f92-d1221f88a3a5"}